<title>GERMANY: Hochtief wins order to build Sony-Center.</title>
<headline>Hochtief wins order to build Sony-Center.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Hochtief AG said on Tuesday it had won an order worth 590 million marks to build Sony Corp's planned Sony-Center building in Berlin.</p>
<p>Hochtief was named as general manager for the project, which will also provide work for Germany's BE-ST Bellevuestrae Development GmbH &amp; Co, U.S.-based Tishman Speyer Properties and Japan's Kajima.</p>
<p>The centre is planned to include seven buildings with over 132,500 square metres of space.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom +49 228 260 97150</p>
